## How to add a git repo in a folder
1. Initialize Git:  $ git init
2. Add files:       $ git add . 
3. Make a commit:   $ git commit -m "first commit"
4. Add remote:      $ git remote add origin "https://url-of-the-repo.git"
5. Push:            $ git push -u origin main

NOTE: Git Submodules (A Repo Inside Another Repo)
Do you want to add a repository as a subdirectory within a project that is already a Git repository?
Then use a submodule. This is useful for libraries or shared tools.

In the terminal, navigate to your main project.

Run this command:
$ git submodule add https://github.com/gebruikersnaam/repository-naam.git path/to/folder

Git will now create a reference to the other repository without simply merging the files.
